From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1ma <hello@1ma.ai>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:46:13 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] 1ma: built-in 1ma plugins take over verified installed copies

Before patch 0014 the 1ma plugins were installed from 1ma's repository (git)
or from the Linux release folder (path). When a built-in 1ma plugin meets a
copy with its id, reconcileBundled now moves that row to the built-in source
instead of skipping it, keeping the enablement and, through the plugin id,
the settings, secrets, schedules and data. Only a verifiable 1ma source
qualifies: git from github.com/1ma-ai/1ma with subdirectory plugins/<name>,
or a folder carrying the release script's .1ma-release.json; a copy newer
than the built-in is kept. Every other copy stays and the log says why.
Before the first takeover the database is copied to
<data>/backups/before-1ma-builtins-<version>-<time>.db: an app from before
0014 deletes these rows at start, so going back means restoring that copy.
---
 .../services/plugins/plugin-registration.ts   | 109 ++++++++++++++++-
 .../services/plugins/plugin-service.test.ts   | 111 ++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 219 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

